<div class="poster">

  <!-- ══ HEADER ══ -->
  <div class="header">
    <div class="header-top">
      <span class="journal-badge">Nature · 2024</span>
      <span class="doi-badge">DOI: 10.1038/s41586-024-07487-w</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="poster-title">Mapping Neural Circuit Architecture:<br>Advances in Brain Connectivity Analysis</h1>
    <p class="poster-subtitle">
      A comprehensive large-scale connectomics study revealing new principles of neural circuit organization
      through multi-modal electron microscopy, deep learning reconstruction, and graph-theoretic analysis.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- ══ METRICS BANNER ══ -->
  <div class="metrics-banner">
    <div class="metric-card blue">
      <div class="metric-value">~125K</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Neurons Mapped</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Total neurons reconstructed in connectome dataset</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card teal">
      <div class="metric-value">~54M</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Synaptic Connections</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Individual synapses identified and catalogued</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card gold">
      <div class="metric-value">37</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Circuit Motifs</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Distinct recurring connectivity motifs discovered</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card green">
      <div class="metric-value">94.2%</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Classification Accuracy</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Automated neuron-type classification performance</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ══ BACKGROUND ══ -->
  <div class="section-card full-width">
    <div class="section-label label-blue">01 · Background & Motivation</div>
    <div class="section-title">
      <span class="dot dot-blue"></span>
      Why Map Neural Circuits at Scale?
    </div>
    <p class="bg-text">
      Understanding how the brain processes information requires detailed maps of neural connectivity. Classical neuroanatomy provided foundational insights, but the field lacked the resolution and scale needed to capture complete circuit-level wiring diagrams. Recent convergence of <strong style="color:#93c5fd">electron microscopy, automated segmentation, and computational neuroscience</strong> makes large-scale connectomics feasible for the first time. This landmark 2024 <em>Nature</em> study reconstructs and analyzes neural circuits at unprecedented scale—bridging the gap between structural connectivity and functional organization.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- ══ METHODS PIPELINE ══ -->
  <div class="section-card full-width">
    <div class="section-label label-teal">02 · Methodology & Technical Approach</div>
    <div class="section-title">
      <span class="dot dot-teal"></span>
      Multi-Modal Connectomics Pipeline
    </div>
    <div class="pipeline">
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-icon">🔬</div>
        <div class="step-label">Imaging</div>
        <div class="step-detail">Serial-section EM<br>4 × 4 × 30 nm resolution</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-icon">🧠</div>
        <div class="step-label">Segmentation</div>
        <div class="step-detail">Deep learning neuron tracing + human proofreading</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-icon">⚡</div>
        <div class="step-label">Synapse Detection</div>
        <div class="step-detail">CNN classifier 94.2% accuracy</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-icon">🕸️</div>
        <div class="step-label">Circuit Analysis</div>
        <div class="step-detail">Graph-theoretic motif detection & clustering</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-icon">✅</div>
        <div class="step-label">Validation</div>
        <div class="step-detail">Calcium imaging + optogenetic perturbation</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Pipeline Component</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Imaging</td>
          <td>Serial-section electron microscopy at 4 nm × 4 nm × 30 nm voxel resolution</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Segmentation</td>
          <td>Deep learning-based automated neuron tracing with expert human proofreading</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Synapse Detection</td>
          <td>Convolutional neural network classifier achieving 94.2% accuracy</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Circuit Analysis</td>
          <td>Graph-theoretic motif detection and graph clustering algorithms</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Functional Validation</td>
          <td>Calcium imaging and optogenetic perturbation experiments</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <!-- ══ KEY FINDINGS ══ -->
  <div class="section-card full-width">
    <div class="section-label label-gold">03 · Key Findings</div>
    <div class="section-title">
      <span class="dot dot-gold"></span>
      Principal Discoveries in Neural Circuit Organization
    </div>
    <div class="findings-grid">

      <div class="finding-card highlight-gold">
        <div class="finding-stat">37</div>
        <div class="finding-title">Distinct Connectivity Motifs</div>
        <div class="finding-desc">
          37 recurring connectivity motifs identified as modular building blocks of larger circuits, suggesting a finite "vocabulary" of circuit elements analogous to logic gates in digital circuits.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="finding-card highlight-blue">
        <div class="finding-stat">3.5% → 28%</div>
        <div class="finding-title">Hub Neuron Disproportionate Influence</div>
        <div class="finding-desc">
          Hub neurons comprising only <strong style="color:#93c5fd">3.5% of the population</strong> account for over <strong style="color:#93c5fd">28% of total synaptic output</strong>—a highly non-uniform distribution of influence across the network.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="finding-card highlight-teal">
        <div class="finding-stat">4.7:1</div>
        <div class="finding-title">Layer 5 Recurrent-to-Feedforward Ratio</div>
        <div class="finding-desc">
